notes={
375812:('HOLD_FULL_PARTITION_REGULARITY_GAP','Source Conjecture 1.1 and Theorem 1.2 read. Multiplicative-function level sets do not encode arbitrary finite colorings. The parametrization (2mn,m^2-n^2,m^2+n^2) preserves the equation but does not ensure equal colors. Need recurrence for arbitrary color classes; neither two-color results nor two coincident entries settle every finite coloring. Natural numbers here mean the source positive domain; a zero triple would be a domain correction, zero credit.'),
361909:('EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_REFUTATION','Theorem 5.2 and proof of Chudnovsky–Trotignon, current arXiv:2405.07471, read. Explicit superlinear F specialization gives hereditary polynomial (tw,omega)-bounded class of unbounded tree-independence. Full earlier-result bridge in ORDINARY.md. Journal PDF denied; no retry. Published result, not a new candidate.'),
362991:('EXCLUDE_LITERAL_HYPOTHESIS_CORRECTION','Identity has whole-group centralizer of index one, contradicting the literal hypothesis for every element. Full vacuity proof and correct FC-center definition in ORDINARY.md. The source amenable result does not prove the general corrected conjecture.'),
358072:('HOLD_SUBFACTOR_RECONSTRUCTION_GAP','Source Conjecture 1.1 and surrounding classification read: k=2,3,4 theorems are established there. A permutation-group classification is insufficient: Goldman-type reconstruction concerns recognizing the group-subgroup subfactor from standard invariant data. Need the exact recognition theorem for all remaining sharp cases, including sharply 5-transitive M12, not merely a group action enumeration. No new full route.'),
358902:('HOLD_QUASI_POWER_CONTRACTION_GAP','Source Conjectures 2.22/2.23 and explanatory text read. For representable matroids ordinary symmetric tensor rank has the desired dimension, but arbitrary symmetric quasi powers are not assumed representable. Induction requires existence of e for which contracting e Sym_(d-1)(E) preserves the quasi-power restrictions. The flat condition alone was not proved to imply this. Stronger source characterization is not a complete bridge.'),
360514:('HOLD_UNIFORM_DIMENSION_GAP','Actual source Section 12, Conjecture 12.1 read after distinguishing its table of contents. Each X being Ramsey supplies d(k,X), not d(k,n). Taking a maximum over finitely many isometry types is invalid: n-point Euclidean configurations have continuously varying shapes. Need uniform control over those Ramsey configurations or a sequence requiring unbounded dimension; no such mechanism proved.'),
360786:('HOLD_PRIME_FIELD_LIST_RECOVERY_GAP','Actual source Conjecture 1.1 and square-root lower-bound argument read. Evaluation on p points determines a polynomial of degree <p, but that only yields an exponential trivial list bound. For l=1 uniqueness is elementary; l>1 with fixed epsilon requires polynomial list size uniformly in p. Subfield-based counterexamples violate the prime-field hypothesis. No full bound obtained.'),
373057:('EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_EXACT_THEOREM','Zenodo October 14, 2026 Theorems 1.2,1.3, definitions and adjacent CFI derivation actually read from PDF. Exact reduction from proper minor-closed M via an excluded K_t and CFI graphs is in ORDINARY.md. Deep proof not independently audited. No transfer from the different strong-conjecture refutation.'),
382165:('HOLD_HEREDITARY_CLASS_MINIMALITY_GAP','Source introduction and bounded-degree/minor-free structural theorems read; whole t-sail proof not audited. Sparse is not interchangeable with bounded maximum degree or excluding a fixed minor. Selecting an infinite sequence of high-treewidth members does not establish a proper hereditary subclass retaining unbounded treewidth: omitted finite graphs may occur induced in all sufficiently rich members. Need a hereditary thinning theorem or genuine minimal sparse class, neither constructed.'),
375328:('HOLD_COARSE_DECOMPOSITION_GAP','Source introduction, tree decomposition definitions and restricted biclique-induced-minor-free result read. Neighboring fixed-radius source-family historical result r346 reconciled. Recursive balanced separation uses covers of bounded size but separator boundaries can accumulate over logarithmically many levels. Need radius/cover bounds depending only on k,r, not |G|, while preserving connected bag occurrences. Restricted source theorem does not cover all graphs.'),
375527:('HOLD_CLASS_OBSTRUCTION_FINITALITY_GAP','Source limiting-density discussion and explicit below-3/2 class obstructions read. Finiteness of obs(G) for EACH minor-closed class does not imply finiteness of cobs of a property of CLASSES. The latter quantifies over infinitely many distinct classes. Need class-level wqo or density-specific restriction for arbitrary rational delta; the finite below-3/2 classification is not that bridge.'),
375918:('HOLD_GENERAL_PRESCRIBED_MATCHING_GAP','Actual source introduction and two-hole definitions read. Zero-sum necessity: sum of prescribed differences equals sum of all vectors, zero for s>=2. Sufficiency is the literal missing assertion. Hall hyperplane case requires every difference to cross a fixed hyperplane; a general zero-sum list need not admit such a functional. Two-hole solution handles exactly two internal requests, not arbitrary counts. Alternating-cycle exchanges do not yet preserve all previously prescribed multiplicities. No enumeration performed.'),
368520:('HOLD_GENERAL_DIMENSION_GAP','Sustained rank, hyperplane-trace and geometric routes in ORDINARY.md. Complete ordinary proof for n=2,4 only, zero-credit classical parameter cases. Need mixed-dimension bound for n>=6. Primary v1/current verified equal; journal redirect is not journal body review.'),
370387:('EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_C5_OBSTRUCTION','Sustained exact witness and failed general greedy-improvement route in ORDINARY.md. C5 with constant four-element lists is 2-degenerate and has no proper conflict-free list coloring, by square graph K5/pigeonhole. Source v2 explicitly states this obstruction before its unqualified Conjecture 4; companion also states it; journal search-body excerpt excludes C5. Full journal PDF timed out. Known/source correction, zero credit.'),
370543:('HOLD_ARBITRARY_ARRANGEMENT_FIDELITY_GAP','Source Theorem 1.2/1.3, tope and separation definitions and proposed reconstruction discussion read. Original Heaviside generators give at least one successful choice; this does not prove EVERY terminal oriented-matroid tope graph is isomorphic to the original. Need uniqueness across generalized Heaviside bases for arbitrary arrangements, beyond the source generic-in-codimension-two theorem. No implementation or basis search.'),
358652:('HOLD_PARAMETER_EXTENSION_SOURCE_MISMATCH','Current v6 torso discussion actually read. It gives p(G,X)<=p^t(G,X), the perimeter-grid obstruction for treewidth and an open classification question. It does not state the literal iff involving functional strict domination of treewidth in that passage. Earlier versions not all reviewed. Need a precise definition of equivalence, annotated minors and necessity/sufficiency for ALL minor-monotone parameters; no source fidelity clearance or endpoint correction credited.'),
368971:('HOLD_WEIGHTED_CYCLIC_FLAT_IDENTITY_GAP','Sustained coefficient, minor-recursion and exact Schubert-expansion routes in ORDINARY.md; companion Theorem 4.3 proof read. Exact missing identity is the signed cyclic-flat sum of basis corner counts equaling n t01-2t02. Source worked examples and captions read, no visual figure audit. No shortcut equating derivatives at zero and minus one.'),
358002:('HOLD_ENCOUNTERED_PUBLIC_FULL_SCOPE_CLAIM','Source Conjecture 1, Vandermonde and symmetry passages; 2026 companion and current Hexagon PDF Theorem E/dependency outline read. Theorem E of October 27, 2026 covers ad=bc as a specialization of ad<=bc. Its long analytic and computer-assisted certificate is materially unaudited. No proof validity or novelty clearance inferred from its abstract; encountered claimed subsumer blocks qualification. Full ordinary symmetry bridge in ORDINARY.md.'),
367360:('EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_SOURCE_CORRECTION','Source current Theorem 1.1 read. Seven-vertex double star with center degrees 3,4 and five leaves falls into corrected n+1 case but literal n case. Full scope bridge in ORDINARY.md; switching proof not independently audited. Already published source correction, zero credit.'),
369938:('HOLD_INTERMEDIATE_SUBSET_REGIME_GAP','Source prime-field Conjecture 1.2 and dense/general-group bounds read. F_2^n result does not imply the prime-field endpoint. Greedy distinct partial sums can be trapped in the already used sums and there is no proved exchange invariant to finish. Small subsets and |S|>=p^(1-c) leave an intermediate regime; arbitrary p and every subset are required. No group/set enumeration performed.')}
